{"type":"message","id":"486093b5","parentId":"79e888e0","timestamp":"2026-04-03T07:19:24.932Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b53c2d15a5ca0ee7a516507da96d\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a\",\n  \"sender\": \"ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Fri 2026-04-03 07:19 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a\",\n  \"name\": \"ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b53c2d15a5ca0ee7a516507da96d]\nou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a: \"defaults\": {\n  \"ask\": \"off\"\n}\n这样设置的效果是什么"}],"timestamp":1775200764928}}
{"type":"message","id":"45fc993e","parentId":"486093b5","timestamp":"2026-04-03T07:19:49.583Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about what the effect of setting `\"defaults\": { \"ask\": \"off\" }` in exec-approvals.json would be. They want to know what this configuration does.\n\nBased on what I know about OpenClaw's exec approval system:\n- `ask` controls whether exec command approval is requested\n- `ask: \"off\"` means no approval prompt will be shown - commands will run without asking\n\nBut I should be careful here - I don't have definitive knowledge that `ask: \"off\"` is a valid field in exec-approvals.json's defaults section. The exec-approvals.json file seems to be about allowlisting specific commands, and I'm not 100% sure if `ask` is a valid configuration there.\n\nThe user previously mentioned seeing this pattern:\n```json\n\"defaults\": {\n  \"security\": \"full\",\n  \"ask\": \"off\"\n}\n```\n\nAnd they wanted to add these rules. I should explain what I understand the effect would be, but also note that I'm not 100% certain this is the correct structure for exec-approvals.json since it seems to be primarily for command allowlisting.","thinkingSignature":"e8739da20e752a657b5ba135b90acb55221f239d689e5215142b96d2618add16"},{"type":"text","text":"<final>\n根据 OpenClaw 的 exec 授权机制：\n\n### `\"ask\": \"off\"` 的效果\n\n**关闭 exec 命令的授权确认提示** —— 执行命令时不再弹出 `Do you approve this command?` 的对话框，命令直接执行。\n\n### 举个例子\n\n不加这个的时候，你执行 `exec` 会弹：\n```\n/approve 9f885561 allow-once|allow-always|deny\n```\n\n加了 `ask: \"off\"` 之后，匹配的命令直接跑，不等你点批准。\n\n---\n\n### 但有个问题\n\n你的 `exec-approvals.json` 目前的结构是：\n```json\n{\n  \"defaults\": {},\n  \"agents\": { ... }\n}\n```\n\n`defaults` 目前是空的。加 `\"ask\": \"off\"` 是否生效，**取决于这个文件是否支持 `ask` 字段**。\n\n我之前没能确认是因为文档目录访问超时了。\n\n---\n\n### 建议\n\n1. **先备份**：cp 一份 `exec-approvals.json`\n2. **小范围试**：先在一个不重要的 agent 上试，别直接加在 `defaults`\n3. **或者先问**：在 OpenClaw 社区/Discord 确认下 `ask` 字段是不是加在 `exec-approvals.json` 里的\n\n你想试吗？\n</final>"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"minimax-m2.5:free","usage":{"input":39,"output":508,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":21066,"totalTokens":21613,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775200764931,"responseId":"061e9cfdb4878a202bc49381dd1c58c0"}}
